    "updated_at": "2022-09-10T16:50:47Z",
    "body": "Yeah, @keithamus is correct. Dictionary members can be detected quite well in most cases.\r\n\r\nThere's another thread on timeouts (see the issues with the same label) and one question I have is whether this should perhaps be a subclass of sorts as you probably also want to give the controller access to adjusting the timeout value, canceling it, and perhaps resetting it. Maybe it's okay to put all that on `AbortController` directly, but we'd have to think it through a bit.",
